  SRAM CIM vs von Neumann at reuse 1: 23.9x better
  SRAM CIM vs von Neumann at reuse 1000: 2.6x
  RRAM CIM vs von Neumann at reuse 1: 16.5x better
  RRAM CIM vs von Neumann at reuse 1000: 1.8x

The CIM columns do not move with reuse because they never fetch
a weight. That gap IS the O(1)-MAC advantage, and it is only
visible against a machine that does fetch. Comparing SRAM CIM
against ReRAM CIM cannot show it, because both already have it.

Note the baseline is optimistic: no control logic, no
instruction fetch, no clock distribution. A real digital
accelerator would do worse, so this is a lower bound on the
advantage.

